    "unmatched_normalized_lines": [],
    "coordinate_note": "Input-file line matches; upstream spans address normalized text. Degraded positions are not original-source positions."
  },
  {
    "window_id": "e7a2f0c6-6a45-5300-a8e2-33698b083c57",
    "source_id": "sgb-scrapy024-feed-exports",
    "input_sha256": "a3831d75f00d59a0527a469dc26af5dcf741294e25572c46bb587b28f7e2165d",
    "official_span": {
      "start": 870,
      "end": 1162
    },
    "exact_line_matches": [
      {
        "input_line": 24,
        "text": "For serializing the scraped data, the feed exports use the [Item exporters](exporters.html#topics-exporters). These formats are supported out of the box:"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 26,
        "text": "- JSON"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 27,
        "text": "- JSON lines"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 28,
        "text": "- CSV"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 29,
        "text": "- XML"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 31,
        "text": "But you can also extend the supported format through the"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 32,
        "text": "`FEED_EXPORTERS` setting."
      }
    ],
    "unmatched_normalized_lines": [
      "Serialization formats"
    ],
    "coordinate_note": "Input-file line matches; upstream spans address normalized text. Degraded positions are not original-source positions."
  },
  {
    "window_id": "ec7333ab-7789-5c91-8198-c58e0a938f37",
    "source_id": "sgb-scrapy024-feed-exports",
    "input_sha256": "a3831d75f00d59a0527a469dc26af5dcf741294e25572c46bb587b28f7e2165d",
    "official_span": {
      "start": 1080,
      "end": 2737
    },
    "exact_line_matches": [
      {
        "input_line": 31,
        "text": "But you can also extend the supported format through the"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 32,
        "text": "`FEED_EXPORTERS` setting."
      },
      {
        "input_line": 36,
        "text": "- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `json`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 37,
        "text": "- Exporter used: [`JsonItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.JsonItemExporter)"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 38,
        "text": "- See [this warning](exporters.html#json-with-large-data) if you’re using JSON with"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 39,
        "text": "large feeds."
      },
      {
        "input_line": 43,
        "text": "- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `jsonlines`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 44,
        "text": "- Exporter used: [`JsonLinesItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.JsonLinesItemExporter)"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 48,
        "text": "- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `csv`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 49,
        "text": "- Exporter used: [`CsvItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.CsvItemExporter)"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 50,
        "text": "- To specify columns to export, their order and their column names, use"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 51,
        "text": "`FEED_EXPORT_FIELDS`. Other feed exporters can also use this"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 52,
        "text": "option, but it is important for CSV because unlike many other export"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 53,
        "text": "formats CSV uses a fixed header."
      },
      {
        "input_line": 57,
        "text": "- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `xml`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 58,
        "text": "- Exporter used: [`XmlItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.XmlItemExporter)"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 62,
        "text": "- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `pickle`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 63,
        "text": "- Exporter used: [`PickleItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.PickleItemExporter)"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 67,
        "text": "- Value for the `format` key in the `FEEDS` setting: `marshal`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 68,
        "text": "- Exporter used: [`MarshalItemExporter`](exporters.html#scrapy.exporters.MarshalItemExporter)"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 72,
        "text": "When using the feed exports you define where to store the feed using one or multiple [URIs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniform_Resource_Identifier)"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 73,
        "text": "(through the `FEEDS` setting). The feed exports supports multiple"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 74,
        "text": "storage backend types which are defined by the URI scheme."
      }
    ],
    "unmatched_normalized_lines": [
      "JSON",
      "JSON lines",
      "CSV",
      "XML",
      "Pickle",
      "Marshal",
      "Storages"
    ],
    "coordinate_note": "Input-file line matches; upstream spans address normalized text. Degraded positions are not original-source positions."
  },
  {
    "window_id": "8cae5065-db47-54bb-aa9d-4857f5bf262c",
    "source_id": "sgb-scrapy024-feed-exports",
    "input_sha256": "a3831d75f00d59a0527a469dc26af5dcf741294e25572c46bb587b28f7e2165d",
    "official_span": {
      "start": 2739,
      "end": 3253
    },
    "exact_line_matches": [
      {
        "input_line": 76,
        "text": "The storages backends supported out of the box are:"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 78,
        "text": "- Local filesystem"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 79,
        "text": "- FTP"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 80,
        "text": "- S3 (requires [boto3](https://github.com/boto/boto3))"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 81,
        "text": "- Google Cloud Storage (GCS) (requires [google-cloud-storage](https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/reference/libraries#client-libraries-install-python))"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 82,
        "text": "- Standard output"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 84,
        "text": "Some storage backends may be unavailable if the required external libraries are"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 85,
        "text": "not available. For example, the S3 backend is only available if the [boto3](https://github.com/boto/boto3)"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 86,
        "text": "library is installed."
      }
    ],
    "unmatched_normalized_lines": [],
    "coordinate_note": "Input-file line matches; upstream spans address normalized text. Degraded positions are not original-source positions."
  },
  {
    "window_id": "2ba801a6-b145-5048-a547-15f3ccac9f93",
    "source_id": "sgb-scrapy024-feed-exports",
    "input_sha256": "a3831d75f00d59a0527a469dc26af5dcf741294e25572c46bb587b28f7e2165d",
    "official_span": {
      "start": 3255,
      "end": 3718
    },
    "exact_line_matches": [
      {
        "input_line": 90,
        "text": "The storage URI can also contain parameters that get replaced when the feed is"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 91,
        "text": "being created. These parameters are:"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 93,
        "text": "- `%(time)s` - gets replaced by a timestamp when the feed is being created"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 94,
        "text": "- `%(name)s` - gets replaced by the spider name"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 96,
        "text": "Any other named parameter gets replaced by the spider attribute of the same"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 97,
        "text": "name. For example, `%(site_id)s` would get replaced by the `spider.site_id`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 98,
        "text": "attribute the moment the feed is being created."
      }
    ],
    "unmatched_normalized_lines": [
      "Storage URI parameters"
    ],
    "coordinate_note": "Input-file line matches; upstream spans address normalized text. Degraded positions are not original-source positions."
  },
  {
    "window_id": "601fd9d3-3489-5cf6-90f1-00e4a49d0fe5",
    "source_id": "sgb-scrapy024-feed-exports",
    "input_sha256": "a3831d75f00d59a0527a469dc26af5dcf741294e25572c46bb587b28f7e2165d",
    "official_span": {
      "start": 3720,
      "end": 4115
    },
    "exact_line_matches": [
      {
        "input_line": 100,
        "text": "Here are some examples to illustrate:"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 102,
        "text": "- Store in FTP using one directory per spider:"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 103,
        "text": "  - `ftp://user:password@ftp.example.com/scraping/feeds/%(name)s/%(time)s.json`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 104,
        "text": "- Store in S3 using one directory per spider:"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 105,
        "text": "  - `s3://mybucket/scraping/feeds/%(name)s/%(time)s.json`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 107,
        "text": "[Spider arguments](spiders.html#spiderargs) become spider attributes, hence"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 108,
        "text": "they can also be used as storage URI parameters."
      }
    ],
    "unmatched_normalized_lines": [],
    "coordinate_note": "Input-file line matches; upstream spans address normalized text. Degraded positions are not original-source positions."
  },
  {
    "window_id": "5a26d374-042e-5afe-bc53-91153ef7ccbb",
    "source_id": "sgb-scrapy024-feed-exports",
    "input_sha256": "a3831d75f00d59a0527a469dc26af5dcf741294e25572c46bb587b28f7e2165d",
    "official_span": {
      "start": 4117,
      "end": 4547
    },
    "exact_line_matches": [
      {
        "input_line": 114,
        "text": "The feeds are stored in the local filesystem."
      },
      {
        "input_line": 116,
        "text": "- URI scheme: `file`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 117,
        "text": "- Example URI: `file:///tmp/export.csv`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 118,
        "text": "- Required external libraries: none"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 120,
        "text": "Note that for the local filesystem storage (only) you can omit the scheme if"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 121,
        "text": "you specify an absolute path like `/tmp/export.csv` (Unix systems only)."
      },
      {
        "input_line": 122,
        "text": "Alternatively you can also use a [`pathlib.Path`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.Path) object."
      }
    ],
    "unmatched_normalized_lines": [
      "Local filesystem"
    ],
    "coordinate_note": "Input-file line matches; upstream spans address normalized text. Degraded positions are not original-source positions."
  },
  {
    "window_id": "048437eb-be39-5ac9-996f-ed6d287dc99e",
    "source_id": "sgb-scrapy024-feed-exports",
    "input_sha256": "a3831d75f00d59a0527a469dc26af5dcf741294e25572c46bb587b28f7e2165d",
    "official_span": {
      "start": 4549,
      "end": 4967
    },
    "exact_line_matches": [
      {
        "input_line": 126,
        "text": "The feeds are stored in a FTP server."
      },
      {
        "input_line": 128,
        "text": "- URI scheme: `ftp`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 129,
        "text": "- Example URI: `ftp://user:pass@ftp.example.com/path/to/export.csv`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 130,
        "text": "- Required external libraries: none"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 132,
        "text": "FTP supports two different connection modes: [active or passive](https://stackoverflow.com/a/1699163). Scrapy uses the passive connection"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 133,
        "text": "mode by default. To use the active connection mode instead, set the"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 134,
        "text": "`FEED_STORAGE_FTP_ACTIVE` setting to `True`."
      }
    ],
    "unmatched_normalized_lines": [
      "FTP"
    ],
    "coordinate_note": "Input-file line matches; upstream spans address normalized text. Degraded positions are not original-source positions."
  },
  {
    "window_id": "189cb074-e02b-5852-b10f-6e4aaa02da95",
    "source_id": "sgb-scrapy024-feed-exports",
    "input_sha256": "a3831d75f00d59a0527a469dc26af5dcf741294e25572c46bb587b28f7e2165d",
    "official_span": {
      "start": 5205,
      "end": 5603
    },
    "exact_line_matches": [
      {
        "input_line": 146,
        "text": "The feeds are stored on [Amazon S3](https://aws.amazon.com/s3/)."
      },
      {
        "input_line": 148,
        "text": "- URI scheme: `s3`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 149,
        "text": "- Example URIs:"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 150,
        "text": "  - `s3://mybucket/path/to/export.csv`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 151,
        "text": "  - `s3://aws_key:aws_secret@mybucket/path/to/export.csv`"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 152,
        "text": "- Required external libraries: [boto3](https://github.com/boto/boto3) >= 1.20.0"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 154,
        "text": "The AWS credentials can be passed as user/password in the URI, or they can be"
      },
      {
        "input_line": 155,
        "text": "passed through the following settings:"
      }
    ],
    "unmatched_normalized_lines": [
      "S3"
    ],
    "coordinate_note": "Input-file line matches; upstream spans address normalized text. Degraded positions are not original-source positions."
